---
import LegalLayout from '../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { translations } from '../../../i18n/translations';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const t = translations[lang];
---
<LegalLayout
  lang={lang}
  currentRoute="terms"
  title={`${t.footer.terms} — Kaxa`}
  description={t.meta.description}
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="Last updated: June 10, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    By downloading, installing, or using Kaxa ("the app", "the service") you agree to these Terms
    of Service. If you do not agree with them, you must not use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Description of the service</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa is a personal finance organization app that lets you track expenses and income, organize
    them into pockets, create budgets, track debts, and set savings goals. Kaxa is an
    organizational tool and does not constitute financial, legal, or tax advice.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Subscriptions and pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa offers the following subscription plans, managed through Google Play and/or the App
    Store via RevenueCat:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Weekly plan: $1.99 USD per week, with a 3-day free trial.</li>
    <li>Monthly plan: $4.99 USD per month.</li>
    <li>Yearly plan: $24.99 USD per year (best value).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Prices may vary based on local taxes applied by the app store. Subscriptions renew
    automatically at the end of each period unless cancelled before the renewal date from your
    Google Play or App Store account settings.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    The weekly plan includes a 3-day free trial. If you do not cancel before the trial ends, you
    will be automatically charged the price of the selected plan.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to use Kaxa only for personal, lawful purposes. You must not attempt to gain
    unauthorized access to Kaxa's systems, reverse-engineer the app, or use it in a way that could
    damage, disable, or overburden the service.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa, its logo, design, and content are owned by its developers. No ownership rights over the
    app are granted by using the service, only a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license
    to use it in accordance with these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa is a personal organization tool. We are not responsible for financial decisions made
    based on information recorded in the app, nor for losses arising from data entry errors,
    technical failures, or service interruptions. The app is provided "as is", without warranties
    of any kind.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to the service</h2>
  <p>
    We may modify, suspend, or discontinue features of Kaxa at any time. If a change
    significantly affects your subscription, we will try to notify you with reasonable advance
    notice.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using Kaxa and cancel your subscription at any time from the corresponding app
    store. We may suspend or terminate access for accounts that violate these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Honduras, without prejudice to the
    consumer protection provisions of your country of residence.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about these Terms of Service, write to us at
    <a href={`mailto:${t.footer.contactEmail}`} class="text-primary underline">{t.footer.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
